{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792429731,"nonce":"q1t94sgTNHLbj7pbrRmW0G2K/Eg=","title":"Open editor tabs held about 28 MB each, and RayDE with ten of them reached 1.2 GB","message":"RayDE with ten tabs open showed 1.1 to 1.22 GB, and took a long time to fall to 860 MB. Measured with a scratch driver that opens one file after another in RayDE's workbench (heap after a major collection, `footprint -p`, `vmmap`).\n\n**Where it went**\n\n- The code minimap's canvas was created with `retain`, so each tab kept its triangles (30 vertices of 7 floats for each run of a row, on the Haxe heap), its paints and its upload bytes for good: about 20 MB a tab. With it off, the canvas gives them back two seconds after its last build. Twelve tabs went from 481 MB to 264 MB of live heap.\n- What stays on the GPU for a minimap is its data table: 69 to 325 rows of 32 KB, 41 MB for ten tabs. A rect costs 30 vertices (60 texels) and a paint (8), because `Sweep` makes a fringe round every fill; a rect that is axis-aligned could be six vertices and the shader's distances.\n- The workbench holds about 18 MB with no project and 122 MB in RayDE's own, 567 tree items (390 folders, 177 sources), about 180 KB for each. RayDE builds every folder's items, collapsed or not, and each `TreeItem` is some ten elements and two layout animations.\n- Opening a tab draws a burst in which graphics memory goes from 8 MB to 230 to 550 MB for a few seconds and falls back; at rest it is 2 to 18 MB. In the burst there are about a hundred sets of a 1 MB and a 0.75 MB allocation, the size of the records upload, which is written whole for each frame.\n- A styled element holds 5 to 20 KB of Haxe heap after its first flush (a class-less div 5.7 KB, one with a component class 15 to 20 KB, a button 84 KB), the main weight of everything above. The cause is not found: what the cascade keeps for it is small (8 fields, a 113 character signature, shared value maps).\n- RayDE rebuilt every open editor each time a file opened, which was 1.8 GB of allocation for the twelfth tab; RayDE's own change (keyed pages) removed that.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- `CodeMinimap` no longer retains its canvas. A render check in `GpuErrorPixels` covers a canvas giving back what it built.\n\n**Next**\n\n- Upload only the rows of the records texture that changed, which the damage comparison knows.\n- Make a tree's collapsed folders cheap: lazy children in `TreeItem`, or an item that builds its row when it scrolls into view.\n- Find what a flush keeps for each element.\n- Draw an axis-aligned rect in six vertices.","files":null}]}